[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: FlightMD stakeholder needs
UID: FMD-STK
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
What the people around FlightMD need from it, taken from the ConOps (`docs/lifecycle/03-system/conops.md`). Needs are validated with the stakeholders, not verified; system requirements (`system-requirements.sdoc`) trace up to them. None has been validated with anyone but the owner yet. The requirements standard (`docs/lifecycle/02-standards/requirements-standard.md`) says how these are written.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: What went wrong, in plain words, with the evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Pilots and maintainers need to learn from one flight log what went wrong in the flight and how bad it is, in plain words, with the numbers and the time in the log that support each statement.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (pilot, maintainer), 4.1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: What to change
STATEMENT: >>>
Tuners need to know which parameter to change, from what value to what value and why, in a form their ground station loads, and need advice that fits their autopilot and frame.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (tuner), 4.2

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Any common log, as recorded
STATEMENT: >>>
Users need to give FlightMD the log their vehicle or ground station wrote (PX4, ArduPilot, MAVLink telemetry, Betaflight or INAV, DJI), compressed or not, without converting it first.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (pilot), 3, 4.1

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A result that can be relied on for what it claims
STATEMENT: >>>
Anyone who acts on a report needs it to be repeatable (the same log gives the same report), to say what it could not check instead of calling it healthy, and to say what it guessed or skipped.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (maintainer, fleet operator), 5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One airframe over time
STATEMENT: >>>
Fleet operators and maintainers need to follow one airframe across flights: trends of the headline numbers, a maintenance log, and whether a change they applied made the finding go away.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (fleet operator), 4.3

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Take the result elsewhere
STATEMENT: >>>
Users need the report and the flight path as files other tools read (PDF, JSON, GPX, KML) and need to compare two flights.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 4.1, 4.4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Use it as an engine
STATEMENT: >>>
Integrators need to run the analysis from their own software (a Python call, a command line, an HTTP API) and need the report format to be versioned and published so a change does not break them silently.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (integrator), 4.4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Logs stay private
STATEMENT: >>>
Users need their logs, tracks and airframe history not to be exposed to others, need to be able to run without any outside network call, and need anything they contribute to be removable.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (pilot, self-hoster), 4.5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A service that stays up
STATEMENT: >>>
Whoever hosts the service needs it to keep working when given huge, damaged or hostile files and too many requests, on a small machine, and to see how it is doing.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (self-hoster), 4.5

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Context of the flight
STATEMENT: >>>
Users need the context a log does not carry when it can be had: where the flight was, the weather that day, and the planning brief the flight was flown against.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 4.1, 3 (planning tool)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Add a check without forking
STATEMENT: >>>
Developers need to add their own health check as a separate package and have it run, be scored and be reported like the built-in ones.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (developer), 4.4

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STK-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Changes to the engine do not change results unnoticed
STATEMENT: >>>
The project's maintainers and everyone who relies on reports need a change to a parser or a rule that alters the result for a real log to be noticed and agreed before it is released.
<<<
SOURCE: ConOps 2 (project maintainer), 5
